rcroft of Norton Priory, near Runcorn, Cheshire, an example of a wine storage area in a historic domestic setting","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorton_Priory_wine_bins.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Doorways_to_service_rooms%2C_Old_Rectory%2C_Warton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_166428.jpg/500px-Doorways_to_service_rooms%2C_Old_Rectory%2C_Warton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_166428.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Doorways_to_service_rooms%2C_Old_Rectory%2C_Warton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_166428.jpg/500px-Doorways_to_service_rooms%2C_Old_Rectory%2C_Warton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_166428.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The classic layout of an important mediaeval house, showing three doorways to service rooms, Old Rectory, Warton. These doorways are here seen from inside the Great Hall, but would originally have been hidden by the wooden screen of the screens passage. The central doorway leads into a passage to an outside  kitchen. The other two doors are to the pantry and buttery","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADoorways_to_service_rooms%2C_Old_Rectory%2C_Warton_-_geograph.org.uk_-_166428.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/The_architectural_history_of_the_University_of_Cambridge%2C_and_of_the_colleges_of_Cambridge_and_Eton_%281886%29_%2814592435568%29.jpg/500px-The_architectural_history_of_the_University_of_Cambridge%2C_and_of_the_colleges_of_Cambridge_and_Eton_%281886%29_%2814592435568%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/The_architectural_history_of_the_University_of_Cambridge%2C_and_of_the_colleges_of_Cambridge_and_Eton_%281886%29_%2814592435568%29.jpg/1280px-The_architectural_history_of_the_University_of_Cambridge%2C_and_of_the